# Cascade — Cursor rules

You are working on Cascade, a single-user finance PWA (Next.js 15 App Router, TS, Tailwind,
Dexie, Serwist). Read CLAUDE.md before making changes.

## Hard rules
- Money is ALWAYS integer minor units (kobo). Never store or compute money as a float.
  Convert/format only at the display boundary via lib/money.ts.
- lib/waterfall.ts must stay PURE (no I/O, no Dexie, no React). Keep its tests green.
  The invariant sum(allocations) + free === inflow must always hold.
- No auth, no backend, no remote DB in v1. Persistence is IndexedDB (Dexie) only.
- Do not add features outside v1 scope (no spend tracking, categories, charts, investing
  picker, sync, login). If you think one is needed, add a `// v2:` comment, don't build it.

## Style
- TypeScript strict, no `any`, no non-null `!` unless justified with a comment.
- Pure logic in lib/, side effects at the edges, components presentational.
- Tailwind only; flat design, primary teal #0D9488; sentence case in UI copy.
- Small, focused commits. After each pass, run typecheck + tests before moving on.

## When unsure
Prefer the smaller solution that ships. This app's value is being opened every day —
guard simplicity over completeness.
